The ten-state fast block `fastBlock δ` of
`theorem/GridTiedConverter/GFM/FullModel/BoundaryLayer.lean` in the ideal design `k_ff = k_dv = 1`,
`Z_v = 0`, every other parameter value with `L_f, C_f, L_g ≠ 0`; normalized parameters
`k_p, k_i, ρ, r, w, c, P, q` as in
`theorem/GridTiedConverter/GFM/FullModel/BoundaryLayerIdeal.lean`. Continuous time, constant
matrices; excluded: everything excluded by the boundary layer of the full-order model.

Source: as `theorem/GridTiedConverter/GFM/FullModel/BoundaryLayerIdeal.lean`: the determinant
was expanded and divided by `k_i q` by exact computer algebra (discovery evidence) and the identity
is checked here by the kernel through the reflective polynomial-identity check of
`theorem/Dynamics/PolyIdentity.lean` (a 7215-term identity: about a minute of kernel time and
4 GB of memory above the imports).

Results.
* `IdealLevel.delta10R` (7215 terms, eight parts; irreducible over `ℚ`, even in `w`, 3277
  negative coefficients) and `IdealLevel.quinticBilharz10_eq`: the last Bilharz determinant of
  the ideal design is `Δ₁₀ = k_i q · IdealLevel.delta10R`; `Params.fastDelta_four_ideal`.
* **`Params.spectrallyStable_fastBlock_iff_ideal_explicit`**: the boundary layer of the ideal
  design is spectrally stable iff `k_p + ρ + r > 0`, `FastLevel.delta4 > 0`,
  `IdealLevel.delta6 > 0`, `IdealLevel.delta8 > 0` and `k_i q · IdealLevel.delta10R > 0`: the
  stability region of the ideal design as five explicit polynomial inequalities.
-/

